// M4: circles and arcs (compare reference/onshape/circle_arc.md and its images). C: center, then a
// point on the circle, with the rubber-band circle and a live "Ø" value along the radius; the
// diameter box opens (Esc skips it). A: start, end (the chord previews), then the bulge, with a
// live "R" value. From a line chain, Shift+A turns the next piece into a tangent arc, after which
// the tool goes back to Line. The Arc ▾ menu offers the tangent arc tool, which starts at the end
// of a line, and the center-point arc (center, start, then the sweep). Q then makes new geometry
// construction: a dashed circle.
